<objective>
Add 14 new compliance frameworks to the frameworks directory to reach feature parity with Probo and Comp AI which both support a much wider range of regional and industry-specific frameworks.

**Implementation approach:** Read one existing framework file (e.g., nist_800_53.json) to confirm the exact JSON schema, then create each new framework file following the same structure.

**Priority order** (most requested by enterprise compliance teams):
1. FedRAMP High (US government — large enterprise demand)
2. ISO 27017 / ISO 27018 (cloud-specific ISO extensions — very common)
3. OWASP Top 10 (developer teams, widely recognized)
4. BSI C5 (Germany — EU enterprise)
5. TISAX (automotive — large vertical)
6. MAS TRM (Singapore financial — APAC)
7. FFIEC (US financial — banking)
8. ENS (Spain government)
9. IRAP (Australia government)
10. RBI CSF (India financial)
11. KISA ISMS (South Korea)
12. TIC 3.0 (US government network)
13. AWS Well-Architected Security Pillar

**Schema to follow:**
```json
{
  "id": "iso_27017",
  "name": "ISO/IEC 27017:2015",
  "version": "2015",
  "description": "Code of practice for information security controls based on ISO/IEC 27002 for cloud services",
  "controls": [
    {
      "id": "ISO27017-6.3.1",
      "title": "Shared roles and responsibilities within a cloud computing environment",
      "description": "Roles and responsibilities of cloud service customers and cloud service providers shall be defined and documented.",
      "domain": "Organization of Information Security",
      "required": true
    }
  ]
}
```

Output: 14 JSON files in backend/frameworks/, all with meaningful control lists (not stub data)
</objective>
